\section{Retries}{

A statement is sent with a \code{requestId}. If the request has to be sent again,
the same id is sent with \code{retry=true}, and Snowflake does not run the
statement a second time if it already ran. So a retried \code{INSERT} does not
write its rows twice. Only temporary failures are retried; a SQL error, 400,
401 (after one credential refresh) and 403 are not. See
\link{skiLift-options} for the limits.
